{"causes": ["The ongoing Second Punic War created an urgent demand for experienced military leaders and consuls within the Roman Republic.", "Quintus Fabius Maximus inherited a powerful political network and a distinguished family name from his father, Quintus Fabius Maximus Verrucosus.", "The Roman system of elected magistracies provided a structured pathway for aristocratic individuals like Maximus to ascend to positions of power."], "effects": ["His consulship contributed to the sustained Roman military effort against Hannibal's forces in southern Italy during a critical phase of the Second Punic War.", "His career ensured the continued political prominence and influence of the Fabia gens within the Roman Republic during a period of national crisis.", "His service alongside his father reinforced the Roman ideal of intergenerational commitment to public duty and military leadership."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "second-punic-war", "sourceName": "Second Punic War", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "quintus-fabius-maximus", "targetName": "Quintus Fabius Maximus", "context": "The career and consulship of Quintus Fabius Maximus occurred during the protracted conflict of the Second Punic War (218–201 BC)."}, {"sourceSlug": "quintus-fabius-maximus", "sourceName": "Quintus Fabius Maximus", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "roman-consulship", "targetName": "Roman Consulship", "context": "Quintus Fabius Maximus held the esteemed office of Roman Consul in 213 BC, sharing the magistracy with Tiberius Sempronius Gracchus."}, {"sourceSlug": "quintus-fabius-maximus", "sourceName": "Quintus Fabius Maximus", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "quintus-fabius-maximus-verrucosus", "targetName": "Quintus Fabius Maximus Verrucosus", "context": "Quintus Fabius Maximus served alongside his father, Quintus Fabius Maximus Verrucosus, during segments of the Second Punic War."}, {"sourceSlug": "roman-republic", "sourceName": "Roman Republic", "verb": "OCCURS_IN